WHY THIS LICENCE, AND NOT THE ORIGINAL'S

`Ophis_v12_Windows.exe` shipped under "LICENSE — Use & Share, No Derivatives
(v1.0)", which withheld modification, derivative works, ports and forks absent
written permission. The copyright in that work is held by the same person who
commissioned this rebuild, so it is relicensed here deliberately rather than by
oversight.

No Derivatives contradicted what this repository is for. It is built to be
modified — `docs/MODDING.md` exists to explain how, and `package.json`
describes it in those words. A licence forbidding the thing the documentation
teaches would be a licence nobody could follow. ShareAlike keeps the intent
that mattered (adaptations stay open on the same terms) and drops the part that
did not.

Previously `package.json` declared "MIT" with no licence file present, over a
codebase whose only written licence said the opposite. That mismatch is
recorded in `docs/reverse/18-official-technical-docs.md` section 7.11, and this
file is the correction.


WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS

The work of this rebuild: everything under `src/`, `tests/`, `tools/` and
`docs/`, the HTML entry points, the generated single-file build, and the prose
of the documentation.

The offline map tiles under `assets/map/` are the original program's own tiles,
copied byte for byte. They are under the same copyright as the rest and so are
covered here.


WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER

Three things travel with this repository under terms that are not this licence,
and this licence does not purport to grant rights in them.

1. THE TYPEFACES. `src/styles/fonts/` and the data URIs inlined into the
   single-file build carry three families, each under the SIL Open Font
   License 1.1, which permits this redistribution:

     Cinzel         Natanael Gama
     EB Garamond    Georg Duffner, Octavio Pardo
     IBM Plex Mono  Mike Abbink, Bold Monday, for IBM

   The copyright notice and the licence text both travel with them, as the
   OFL requires: `src/styles/fonts/OFL.txt` in this tree, and reproduced as a
   comment in `src/styles/fonts.css` so that it is also inside
   `ophis-single.html`, which embeds the faces as data URIs and leaves here on
   its own. A FAQ accompanies the licence at https://openfontlicense.org

2. THE ARCHAIX THESIS. The ideas this instrument renders — the 138 lattice,
   the Phoenix and Nemesis cycles, the palindromic mirror — are the
   copyrighted work of Jason M. Breshears and are not licensed here. What is
   licensed is this project's own expression of them: its code, its measured
   results, and its prose. Summaries are in this project's own words, with
   short attributed quotations.

   As attribution under section 3(a)(1)(A) of the licence below, the framing
   notice must be retained: that this is a study instrument rendering the
   Archaix thesis of Jason M. Breshears, and that it studies software, not
   cosmology. It stands at `README.md` and `docs/WHITEPAPER.md` section 1. This
   is the one requirement carried forward verbatim from the original licence,
   where it was clause (c).

3. THE ECLIPSE DATA. `src/data/eclipses-canon.data.js` is rebuilt from NASA's
   published canon. The source is a work of the United States government;
   astronomical events are facts and not subject to copyright. The rebuilt
   arrangement, and the three corrections applied to it, are this project's own
   and are covered above.


NO WARRANTY, AND ONE HONEST WORD ABOUT WHAT IT DOES

Section 5 below disclaims warranties in the usual legal terms. Plainly: this
projects dates from arithmetic on dates you supply. It does not know the
future, and neither the licence nor the documentation claims it does.


